# =============================================================================
# home-soc-lab — .gitignore
#
# Committed FIRST, before any other file. Git history is permanent: adding a
# pattern here after a file is already tracked does nothing, and deleting a
# secret in a later commit leaves it readable in the earlier one.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. Secrets and environment files ----------------------------------------
# Real credentials live here and must never leave this machine. The lab's SIEM
# passwords go in .env; by week 9 this same pattern holds AWS keys.
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets/
credentials
credentials.*

# ...but DO commit the placeholder template, so a stranger knows which
# variables to set. The leading ! un-ignores a file matched above.
!.env.example

# --- 2. Keys and certificates ------------------------------------------------
# A leaked private key is a permanent door into a system. Revocation is the
# only fix, and it is never quick.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
*.cer
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# --- 3. Terraform (arrives week 12, but the habit starts now) ----------------
# State files record your real infrastructure AND store secrets in plain
# readable text. This is one of the most common serious leaks in public repos.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
crash.log

# --- 4. Container runtime data -----------------------------------------------
# Wazuh's indexer writes gigabytes of database files here. Not secret, but
# committing them makes the repo too big to clone — which breaks the entire
# point of this project.
data/
volumes/
wazuh-data/
*-data/
config/wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs/

# --- 5. Downloaded attack datasets -------------------------------------------
# Replayed Windows telemetry is FETCHED BY SCRIPT at a pinned version, never
# committed. Large binaries in git history are permanent dead weight.
datasets/raw/
*.evtx
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# --- 6. Python (the week-2 CLI, and any helper scripts here) -----------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- 7. Editor and OS noise --------------------------------------------------
# Harmless, but it makes a repo look careless. .DS_Store is macOS storing your
# folder's icon positions — it has no business in a security lab.
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# --- 8. Logs and scratch -----------------------------------------------------
*.log
tmp/
scratch/
